(10,'KEEP',[VI,VII,IX],'theory','Testing nonrelativistic covariance of Maxwell and constitutive equations','The actual hint starts with covariance of the ordinary Lorentz force under Galilean coordinates, then explicitly names E/B Maxwell equations and D=epsilon*E,H=B/mu. Transforming derivatives and testing these relations is classical EM mathematics. The final request only sketches a search for a true symmetry/Lorentz transformation; it does not require applying unsupplied relativistic particle kinematics and remains peripheral to the main contradiction.'),
(11,'BORDERLINE',[X],'theory','Image construction for an arbitrarily moving parabolic mirror','Ordinary ray construction with a moving boundary supplies substantial optics, but the source asks an observer-frame image of a rest-frame object at arbitrary v without a small-v convention or Lorentz/aberration relations. The intended Newtonian versus relativistic imaging model is unresolved; retain the whole-task ambiguity.'),
(12,'KEEP',[VI],'theory','Charge distribution of a fully defined complex-shift Coulomb potential','All real/conjugate potentials, Poisson source definition, square-root branch requirement and complex orthogonal matrix condition are printed. Distributional derivatives, support and symmetry are specified mathematics on electrostatics. The last Lorentz-group relationship is a mathematical comparison, not an unsupplied physical boost needed for the charge calculation.'),
(13,'KEEP',[I,VI,VII,IX],'theory','Nonrelativistic Maxwell equations in rotating coordinates','The task explicitly says nonrelativistic, supplies angular velocity and rationalized-cgs convention, and asks transformation of standard Maxwell, continuity and Newton point-charge laws. Rotating derivative/potential calculus gives wave dispersion; approximate charge-pair circular equilibrium and the meaning of neglecting radiation use ordinary classical EM and mechanics.'),
(14,'KEEP',[IV],'theory','Thermal tangent-angle probability for hair with supplied curvature energy','The hair is expressly unstretchable, self-crossing and on the surface, with energy per length proportional to curvature squared. Ordinary classical Boltzmann thermal weighting of this defined energy and Gaussian angular increments determine the endpoint-angle distribution under a declared stiffness/angle convention; no unsupplied polymer kinetic law is needed.'),
(15,'KEEP',[],'theory','Linear concentration profile under a fully supplied diffusion PDE','The statement defines concentration time derivative proportional to the Laplacian and the linear profile. Laplacian zero explains the interior steady solution; conservation and boundary flux distinguish fixed concentrations from an isolated plate. No microscopic diffusion law must be supplied externally.'),
(16,'KEEP',[],'theory','Lattice first-passage probabilities with explicit pedestrian and vehicle rules','Both transition rules, blocked edge, initial directions and absorbing return/home events are printed. Markov recurrences or numerical random-walk sampling yield the probability; only probability mathematics is needed.'),
(17,'REJECT',[],'theory','Relative velocity of superluminal tachyons','Speeds and directions are stated but no Lorentz velocity-addition or admissible tachyon frame prescription is supplied. That unsupplied relativistic rule is the entire requested comparison; a superluminal object also lacks a conventional rest frame.'),
(18,'REJECT',[],'numerical','Proper acceleration, ageing and photon-rocket fuel logistics','Orbit size and onboard acceleration are supplied, but proper acceleration/time, relativistic circular motion and photon-rocket mass-loss relations are not. Those outside laws control station ageing and every robot fuel/timing calculation.'),
(19,'REJECT',[],'theory','Accelerating laser cavity under surface, bulk and gravitational forcing','No gravitational/proper-frame frequency-shift prescription or elastic cavity response model is supplied. Comparing all laser properties and force origins centrally requires relativistic accelerated-frame/gravity and unsupplied solid stress response; ordinary stationary cavity optics alone cannot answer the whole question.'),
(20,'REJECT',[],'theory','Waves in an arbitrarily moving dielectric medium','Rest material epsilon/mu are stated, but moving constitutive relations and Lorentz field/frequency transformation are not. They determine the requested source-frame dispersion, stationary waves and polarizations; ordinary stationary-medium Maxwell equations alone do not operationally supply this relativistic model.'),
(21,'REJECT',[],'theory','Lab-frame distributions from a supplied muon rest-decay spectrum','The rest-frame f(x) and general anisotropic distribution are explicitly supplied. However, rest-to-lab four-momentum boost, massive mass shell and phase-space/Jacobian transformation are not; those outside prerequisites centrally determine both lab distributions.'),
(22,'BORDERLINE',[IV,IX,XI],'theory','Whole photon-gas comparison across a box, free radiation and cosmic expansion','Radiation pressure, Planck spectrum and ordinary Doppler/work/brightness reasoning cover substantial box and sunlight parts. Cosmological redshift/thermal preservation and massive-photon extension are also meaningful and no scale-factor law/dispersion is supplied. Preserve the balanced whole task rather than rescue its classical subparts or reject all photon thermodynamics.'),
