(32,'KEEP',[I],'theory','Planetary orbits under an explicitly supplied cosmological Newton force','The source explicitly restricts analysis to classical mechanics, defines r=a(t)R and provides F=m*(a-double-dot/a)*r in addition to local forces. Newton central-force ODEs, conserved angular momentum and mathematical analytic/numerical study solve all expansion cases. No cosmological field equation or metric is needed.'),
(33,'REJECT',[],'numerical','Neutrino mass from ultra-high-energy Z production and proton decay','The stationary target, proton CM energy fraction and angular law are supplied. Invariant collision energy and boosted daughter energy/direction are not; unsupplied SR reaction kinematics centrally determine both the mass estimate and beam-proposal sensitivity. Printed exotic names alone are not the rejection reason.'),
